title: Sliders drawn with pictures
intro: A Slider takes the same pictures as a Bar, plus one for its handle: a fill that is cut off where it's set, a track that stretches like a nine-slice panel, and a knob of your own.
project: Empty | Slider Images
write: Sprites/gauge.png | bar-images/gauge.png
write: Sprites/frame.png | bar-images/frame.png

chapter: A fill picture | Fill Image
create: Slider
rename: Volume
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
set: Slider.Size = 6, 1
set: Slider.Value = 0.5
look: 0, 0, 2.5
say: Here's a slider, set halfway, drawn in plain colors as sliders always have been.
pickimage: Slider.FillImage = Sprites/gauge.png
set: Slider.Fill = #FFFFFF
explain: field:Slider.FillImage | Fill Image | Give it a Fill Image. It's laid over the whole slider and shown only as far as it's set, cut off rather than squeezed, and the Fill color tints it.
play
expectdrawn: -1.5, 0 = lit
stop

chapter: A framed track | Background Image
pickimage: Slider.BackgroundImage = Sprites/frame.png
set: Slider.Background = #FFFFFF
set: Slider.BackgroundSlice = 0.125
set: Slider.BackgroundSliceSize = 0.125
explain: field:Slider.BackgroundImage | Background Image | The Background Image is the track behind the fill, tinted by the Background color. Background Slice makes it a nine-slice, so its corners keep their shape however long the slider is.
play
expectdrawn: 1.5, 0 = dark
stop

chapter: A knob picture | Knob Image
pickimage: Slider.KnobImage = Sprites/frame.png
explain: field:Slider.KnobImage | Knob Image | The Knob Image replaces the handle at the end of the filled part, tinted by the Knob color. Dragging and clicking work exactly as before.
say: With no pictures set, a slider is plain colors, just as before.
